On Thu, May 2, 2013 at 8:02 PM, Ian Johnson <blindbravado@gmail.com> wrote:

> This amounts to saying it can be local or nonlocal, but doesn't specify
> how to *explicitly* state the distinction. The ability to make such
> specifications (if the language supports them at all) is pretty much my
> third axiom for Lojban design :)
>
>
I don't think the language supports that disticntion via grammar (it can
make it semantically just as you are making it in English, of course). If
you want a grammatical support for the distinction, I guess the first step
would be to show why it would be desirable. Just because a distinction can
be made is not reason enough to make it.

(What are your other axioms?)

